WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:04.960
Wonder Woman might be one of the most powerful
beings in the DC universe, but one of her

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.960
costumes in Zack Snyder’s Justice League,
now streaming on HBO Max, really pushes the

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.680
boundaries of believability.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.150
After receiving a message from her mother,
Queen Hippolyta , in the aftermath of an attack

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.759
in Themyscira , Diana Prince travels from
Paris to the ancient Shrine of the Amazons.

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:23.599
Clad in a crisp white trench coat and heels,
Diana explores the ruins, discovering a distinct

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:24.599
arrow.

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:28.169
Quickly, Diana crafts a makeshift torch and
drops down into a mysterious and shrouded

00:00:28.169 --> 00:00:32.310
tomb to explore it and read the runes beneath
the surface ... but for some reason, Diana

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:36.920
makes that drop in impeccable white stiletto
heels, landing perfectly without hurting herself

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.829
or even damaging her footwear.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:42.789
There's no question that Diana, an Amazonian
goddess with super strength and a whole host

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:46.370
of incredible powers, can do anything she
sets her mind to ... but for anyone who's

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:49.820
ever worn heels in real life, the sequence
is pretty silly.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.879
Fans took to Twitter to share their reactions,
which ranged from mild outrage to complete

00:00:53.879 --> 00:00:55.019
astonishment.

00:00:55.019 --> 00:00:56.019
One user wrote,

00:00:56.019 --> 00:00:59.480
"They couldn't get wonderwoman some more comfortable
shoes for the descent into the center of the

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:00.480
Earth?"

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:01.609
Another user agreed, Tweeting,

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:05.890
"Tell me how WonderWoman jumps down a deep
pit lands on her feet and doesn't break her

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:06.890
heels?

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:07.890
Must be wonder shoes."

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:08.970
Another Twitter user wrote.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.550
“Currently watching the SnyderCut it's certainly
better.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.960
But there's a scene [where] Wonder Woman jumps
down a deep hole while wearing heels.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.190
When she lands they making a gentle 'tap'.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.610
They'd be decimated surely?"

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:20.560
Meanwhile, one user had a simple question:

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.480
"Why does Wonder Woman have to wear heels?"

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.580
In response to comedian Leslie Jones, who
live-tweeted the entire movie and noticed

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.790
that apparently one of Diana's superpowers
is "clean clothes" — referencing her spotless

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.700
white coat — one Twitter user weighed in,
she joked,

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.100
"She's Wonder Woman so of course she has a
constant supply of dirt resistant clothing

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.850
that is made by a high-end designer it is
also the reason that the heels don't break

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.780
off of her shoes and make her fall down."

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.610
However, some fans thought the moment made
Diana even cooler.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:46.610
One user wrote,

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:49.420
"Diana's heels must be one of the most sought
after items by ladies."

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.510
While another user wrote,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:54.170
"The most impressive thing in this movie so
far is wonder woman jumping down hundreds

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:57.640
of feet into the underground cave and landing
with those heels intact."

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:01.210
For some fans, the heels were something they
just couldn't accept; as one Twitter user

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:02.210
put it,

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:04.920
"When aquaman swims in jeans and boots i can
accept it.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.550
but i draw the line at wonder woman wearing
strictly heels."

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:11.880
However, as any action movie fan can tell
you, women performing completely unrealistic

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.350
stunts in spiky, uncomfortable stiletto heels
is nothing new.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:19.500
In recent movies, starlets like Bryce Dallas
Howard, Sienna Miller and Rachel McAdams have

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.370
been forced into a form of footwear that any
woman knows is notorious for their limited

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:27.280
mobility and overt discomfort — and not
only that, they're then tasked with performing

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.580
outrageous action sequences in shoes that
would never withstand a difficult situation.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:36.420
Perhaps the most controversial pair of stiletto
heels in recent memory were Howard's in 2015's

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.390
Jurassic World, where she’s just tottering
around the dangerous park and fleeing dinosaurs

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:44.120
in a pair of patent leather stilettos that
would definitely impede her movement pretty

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.120
intensely.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.880
Eventually, the backlash over Claire's footwear
became so intense that the film's director,

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.380
Colin Trevorrow , was forced to comment, claiming
that Howard herself insisted on the shoes.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.980
Apparently, this was true, and the heels,
which Howard trained in especially for the

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:00.400
role, made a reappearance in the 2018 sequel
Fallen Kingdom.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.710
At least in the movies, heels are certainly
more sturdy than in the real world!

